deko3d (https://github.com/devkitPro/deko3d, zlib) as SwitchWaker vendors it in switch/deko3d
(https://github.com/centollOS/SwitchWaker at 56c0758a4651155ca491ef9d6d3be0ae35be726f, from SwitchWakerHD
bed2af7): the diff of that copy against upstream deko3d 5cc144dcf5606fbcd78430f6c62923546e5f9cf4 (v0.5.0,
the version of devkitPro's libdeko3d.a 0.5.0-1), generated/ left out (build-deko3d.sh takes dekotools'
output from the same SwitchWaker commit). Two fixes, see PATCHES.md (added below): the separate alpha
destination blend factor (dkCmdBufBindBlendStates wrote dstColorBlendFactor into FuncAlphaDst) and the
command buffer's control memory chunks leaked on every clear(). Plus SwitchWaker's CMakeLists.txt
(deko3d_release / deko3d_debug static libraries, upstream Makefile flags).

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2b4978a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# deko3d 0.5.0 (devkitPro, zlib licence) built from source instead of devkitPro's libdeko3d.a, for the
+# fixes in PATCHES.md. Two static libraries, as upstream's Makefile builds them: deko3d_release
+# (-DNDEBUG) and deko3d_debug (-DDEBUG: checks every call, devkitPro's libdeko3dd). generated/ holds
+# what dekodef/dekomme (devkitPro's dekotools) write from source/maxwell/*.def and *.mme (PATCHES.md).
+file(GLOB DEKO3D_SOURCES CONFIGURE_DEPENDS source/*.cpp source/maxwell/*.cpp)
+foreach(variant release debug)
+  add_library(deko3d_${variant} STATIC ${DEKO3D_SOURCES})
+  target_include_directories(deko3d_${variant} PUBLIC include)
+  target_include_directories(deko3d_${variant} PRIVATE generated source source/maxwell)
+  target_compile_definitions(deko3d_${variant} PRIVATE __DK_INTERNAL__)
+  target_compile_options(deko3d_${variant} PRIVATE -O2 -fno-rtti -fno-exceptions -Wall
+                         $<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>:-std=gnu++17>)
+endforeach()
+target_compile_definitions(deko3d_release PRIVATE NDEBUG=1)
+target_compile_definitions(deko3d_debug PRIVATE DEBUG=1)
diff --git a/PATCHES.md b/PATCHES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..be0d4f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PATCHES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# deko3d in SwitchWaker
+
+Copied from SwitchWakerHD (`runtime/third_party/deko3d` at `bed2af7`, centollOS/SwitchWakerHD), patches
+included; the markers keep their name `SwitchWakerHD patch N`. Before, this port linked devkitPro's
+`libdeko3d.a` 0.5.0-1 (the same version). Patch 1 replaced the renderer's `split_alpha` workaround (alpha
+drawn in a second pass, removed 2026-10-17).
+
+deko3d 0.5.0, https://github.com/devkitPro/deko3d at `5cc144d` (tag v0.5.0, the version of devkitPro's
+`libdeko3d.a` SwitchWakerHD linked before; LICENSE: zlib). Built by `CMakeLists.txt` (no Makefile) as the
+static libraries `deko3d_release` and `deko3d_debug` (upstream's `libdeko3d` / `libdeko3dd`, same
+`-DNDEBUG` / `-DDEBUG` and `-O2 -fno-rtti -fno-exceptions -std=gnu++17`). Only `include/`, `source/`,
+`LICENSE` and `README.md` are kept.
+
+`generated/` holds what upstream's Makefile writes with devkitPro's dekotools
+(https://github.com/devkitPro/dekotools, `c15523c`), which the devkitA64 image does not ship:
+
+    for d in source/maxwell/*.def; do n=$(basename $d .def)
+        if [[ $n == *_3d ]]; then dekodef -h generated/$n.h -m generated/$n.mme $d
+        else dekodef -h generated/$n.h $d; fi; done
+    dekomme -o generated/mme_macros.h generated/engine_3d.mme $(ls source/maxwell/*.mme | sort)
+
+Rerun it after editing a `.def` or `.mme` file (dekotools builds with meson, bison and flex, e.g. in a
+`debian:bookworm` container).
+
+Every change to upstream files is marked `SwitchWakerHD patch N`.
+
+1. **Separate alpha destination factor** (`source/maxwell/gpu_3d_state.cpp`, `dkCmdBufBindBlendStates`):
+   upstream writes `dstColorBlendFactor` into `FuncAlphaDst`, so a blend state with its own alpha
+   factors blended alpha with the color's destination factor. The Picto Box writes each subject's
+   number into the picture's alpha with color (SRC_ALPHA, ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA) and alpha (ONE, ZERO)
+   (CB_BLEND0_CONTROL 20010504): the alpha stayed 255 and Lenzo never found the subject (issue #7).
+   Issue #12 (place names) was the same bug, worked around in the renderer before. Still unfixed
+   upstream at `350f2b0` (2026-02).
+
+2. **Control memory chunks lost on clear** (`source/dk_cmdbuf.cpp`, `CmdBuf::clear`): the command buffer's
+   control memory comes in 1 KiB chunks kept in a used list (newest first). `clear()` linked only the newest
+   chunk to the free list, overwriting its link to the older ones, so every frame that needed more than one
+   chunk leaked the rest: ~22,000 chunks (21.6 MiB) in a 14-minute warp tour, found with the malloc census
+   (WWHD_HEAP_CENSUS, docs/memory-round2-plan.md); several hundred MiB over a long session. Still unfixed
+   upstream at `350f2b0` (2026-02).
diff --git a/source/dk_cmdbuf.cpp b/source/dk_cmdbuf.cpp
index acceb93..0a545b2 100644
--- a/source/dk_cmdbuf.cpp
+++ b/source/dk_cmdbuf.cpp
@@ -67,7 +67,12 @@ void CmdBuf::clear()
 	// Transfer all used chunks into the free list
 	if (m_ctrlChunkCur)
 	{
-		m_ctrlChunkCur->m_next = m_ctrlChunkFree;
+		// SwitchWakerHD patch 2: the used chunks are a list (newest first, linked by m_next); linking only the
+		// newest one to the free list dropped every older one, 1 KiB each, on each clear
+		CtrlMemChunk* last = m_ctrlChunkCur;
+		while (last->m_next)
+			last = last->m_next;
+		last->m_next = m_ctrlChunkFree;
 		m_ctrlChunkFree = m_ctrlChunkCur;
 		m_ctrlChunkCur = nullptr;
 	}
diff --git a/source/maxwell/gpu_3d_state.cpp b/source/maxwell/gpu_3d_state.cpp
index 0a689d1..738542e 100644
--- a/source/maxwell/gpu_3d_state.cpp
+++ b/source/maxwell/gpu_3d_state.cpp
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@ void dkCmdBufBindBlendStates(DkCmdBuf obj, uint32_t firstId, DkBlendState const
 			getBlendFactorSetting(state.dstColorBlendFactor), // FuncRgbDst
 			state.alphaBlendOp,                               // EquationAlpha
 			getBlendFactorSetting(state.srcAlphaBlendFactor), // FuncAlphaSrc
-			getBlendFactorSetting(state.dstColorBlendFactor)  // FuncAlphaDst
+			getBlendFactorSetting(state.dstAlphaBlendFactor)  // FuncAlphaDst (SwitchWakerHD patch 1: was dstColorBlendFactor)
 		);
 	}
